      "text": [
        ": قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ يَتَزَوَّجُ اَلرَّجُلُ اَلْأَمَةَ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمِ أَهْلِهَا قَالَ \"هُوَ زِنًى إِنَّ اَللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ يَقُولُ:\n۝ فَانْكِحُوهُنَّ بِإِذْنِ أَهْلِهِنَّ ۝ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4560 - Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated from Abu al-Abbas al-Baqbaq, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdillah (as): \"Can a man marry a bondwoman without the knowledge of her owners?\"\nImam (as) said: \"That is considered fornication. Indeed, Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, says:\n'Then marry them with the permission of their owners' (Surah An-Nisa, 4:25).\""
        ]
      }
